       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is double the labeled maximum for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under prescription labeling (1,200 mg/day for OTC use). A single 1600 mg dose is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, and there is no added analgesic benefit.\n\nI can enter one of these instead, if it fits the clinical intent:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the labeled maximum)\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **Ibuprofen 400 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day), which is common for mild to moderate pain\n\nIf you meant 1600 mg total per day, I can enter 400 mg four times daily. Tell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away. You can also add an adjunct such as scheduled acetaminophen if pain control is the goal."
      }
