       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the labeled maximum, and I can't verify the clinical rationale. The dose is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the 3,200 mg/day maximum.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- **Enter the highest labeled dose now.** That is ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day). If the patient needs more anti-inflammatory or analgesic effect, this is the ceiling.\n- **Route the above-label request through your pharmacy or attending process.** A dose this far above the label would normally need a documented override, such as pharmacist review or attending or specialist sign-off, entered through whatever mechanism your hospital uses for that. I can't act as that approval.\n- **Check for a unit or entry error.** If the intended dose was 1,600 mg/day, I can enter 400 mg four times daily.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll enter the order."
